{% comment %}
  Renders a Purelane-style price row: current price, optional struck
  compare-at price, optional savings badge.

  Not a copy of Dawn's own `snippets/price.liquid` — that snippet's output
  (`.price`, `.price__regular`, description-list markup for volume
  pricing) is a different DOM shape than the prototype's minimal
  `strong + s + em` row, so matching the design pixel-for-pixel means
  writing this instead of forcing Dawn's price component into the
  prototype's CSS. Kept deliberately smaller in scope: no volume pricing,
  no unit price — the prototype doesn't show either for these 5 sections.

  Accepts:
  - price: {Number} current price, in shop currency (required unless `product` given)
  - compare_at: {Number} compare-at price (optional)
  - product: {Object} Product; if given, `price`/`compare_at` default to
    product.price / product.compare_at_price (both already integer cents,
    Shopify's native representation)
  - badge: {String} 'percent' renders "33% off", 'save' renders
    "Save {amount}". Omit for no computed badge.
  - badge_text: {String} explicit badge copy, skips the computed text above
  - pill: {Boolean} true renders the badge as a filled pill (shop card,
    combo card); false renders it as plain text (bundle tier has no badge
    at all, so this only matters when a badge is present)
  - wrapper_class: {String} extra class(es) on the wrapping element, on
    top of the shared `pl-price-row` styling — lets each card snippet
    apply its own layout tweaks (e.g. combos use a larger price)

  Usage:
  {% render 'purelane-price', product: product, badge: 'percent', pill: true %}
  {% render 'purelane-price', price: combo.price, compare_at: combo.compare_at_price, badge: 'save', pill: true, wrapper_class: 'pl-combo__price' %}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  if product and price == blank
    assign price = product.price
  endif
  if product and compare_at == blank
    assign compare_at = product.compare_at_price
  endif

  assign on_sale = false
  if compare_at and price and compare_at > price
    assign on_sale = true
  endif

  if badge_text == blank and on_sale
    if badge == 'percent'
      assign pct = compare_at | minus: price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: compare_at | round
      assign badge_text = pct | append: '% off'
    elsif badge == 'save'
      assign save_amount = compare_at | minus: price
      assign save_money = save_amount | money
      assign badge_text = 'Save ' | append: save_money
    endif
  endif
-%}
<div class="pl-price-row{% if pill %} pl-price-row--pill{% endif %}{% if wrapper_class %} {{ wrapper_class }}{% endif %}">
  <strong>{{ price | money }}</strong>
  {%- if on_sale -%}
    <s>{{ compare_at | money }}</s>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if badge_text != blank -%}
    <em>{{ badge_text }}</em>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
